From: Alan Shearer <sakison@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] libroot: fix syslog truncation stack overflow

vsnprintf returns the length that would have been written. When the
message is longer than the buffer the old else branch used that large
value as an index and wrote past the end of the stack buffer.

Clamp the length to what actually fits before the newline check so the
existing logic never indexes outside the buffer.

diff --git a/src/system/libroot/posix/syslog.cpp b/src/system/libroot/posix/syslog.cpp
--- a/src/system/libroot/posix/syslog.cpp
+++ b/src/system/libroot/posix/syslog.cpp
@@ -147,13 +147,19 @@
 	message.priority = priority;
 	strcpy(message.ident, context->ident);
 
-	int length = vsnprintf(message.message, sizeof(buffer)
-		- sizeof(syslog_message), text, args);
+	const int maxLength = sizeof(buffer) - sizeof(syslog_message);
+	int length = vsnprintf(message.message, maxLength, text, args);
+	if (length < 0)
+		length = 0;
+	else if (length >= maxLength)
+		length = maxLength - 1;
+
 	if (message.message + length - buffer < (int32)sizeof(buffer)) {
 		if (length == 0 || message.message[length - 1] != '\n')
 			message.message[length++] = '\n';
-	} else
-		buffer[length - 1] = '\n';
+	} else if (length > 0)
+		message.message[length - 1] = '\n';
 
 	status_t status;
 	do {
